<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en" data-dpl-id="dpl_2WnVXjvgiBSAG4xTLGUJ4LVaXBxo"><head><meta charSet="utf-8" data-next-head=""/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" data-next-head=""/><title data-next-head="">mcp-security MCP server · dev.modelmarket · ProtocolProbe</title><meta name="description" content="dev.modelmarket/mcp-security 1.0.0: “Scan MCP tool definitions for poisoning, look up server history, count tool-list tokens. Free” (publisher&#x27;s words). MCP server by modelmarket.dev. 5 of 5 record checks met (not a safety rating)." data-next-head=""/><link rel="canonical" href="https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/servers/dev.modelmarket/mcp-security" data-next-head=""/><meta name="robots" content="index, follow" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:type" content="website" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:site_name" content="ProtocolProbe" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:url" content="https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/servers/dev.modelmarket/mcp-security" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:title" content="mcp-security MCP server · dev.modelmarket · ProtocolProbe" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:description" content="dev.modelmarket/mcp-security 1.0.0: “Scan MCP tool definitions for poisoning, look up server history, count tool-list tokens. Free” (publisher&#x27;s words). MCP server by modelmarket.dev. 5 of 5 record checks met (not a safety rating)." data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:image" content="https://protocolprobe.com/og/home.png" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:image:height" content="630" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:image:alt" content="ProtocolProbe — The MCP registry checks at publish. We checked again." data-next-head=""/><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" data-next-head=""/><meta name="twitter:title" content="mcp-security MCP server · dev.modelmarket · ProtocolProbe" data-next-head=""/><meta name="twitter:description" content="dev.modelmarket/mcp-security 1.0.0: “Scan MCP tool definitions for poisoning, look up server history, count tool-list tokens. Free” (publisher&#x27;s words). MCP server by modelmarket.dev. 5 of 5 record checks met (not a safety rating)." data-next-head=""/><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://protocolprobe.com/og/home.png" data-next-head=""/><meta name="pp-record" content="m=1&amp;version=1.0.0&amp;status=active&amp;msg=none&amp;asof=2026-10-22T23%3A38%3A19.277Z&amp;removed=0" data-next-head=""/><link rel="icon" href="/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"/><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="48x48"/><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" type="image/png" sizes="32x32"/><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png"/><link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.webmanifest"/><link rel="alternate" type="application/atom+xml" title="ProtocolProbe — reports, corrections and what&#x27;s new" href="/feed.xml"/><meta name="theme-color" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" content="#f7f6f2"/><meta name="theme-color" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" content="#0e0f11"/><link rel="preload" href="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/0q6bmudldbngt.css" as="style"/><script src="/js/fold.js" defer="" data-next-head=""></script><script src="/theme.js"></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/0q6bmudldbngt.css" data-n-g=""/><noscript data-n-css=""></noscript></head><body><div id="__next"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://protocolprobe.com/#org","name":"ProtocolProbe","url":"https://protocolprobe.com"},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://protocolprobe.com/#site","url":"https://protocolprobe.com","name":"ProtocolProbe","publisher":{"@id":"https://protocolprobe.com/#org"}}]}</script><header class="border-b border-rule"><a href="#main" class="sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:absolute focus:left-4 focus:top-4 focus:z-10 focus:bg-panel focus:px-3 focus:py-2">Skip to content</a><div class="wrap relative flex h-16 items-center gap-2 min-[360px]:gap-3 sm:gap-4 md:gap-7"><a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-2.5 text-[17px] font-semibold tracking-tight no-underline"><svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 26 26" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="1" y="1" width="24" height="24" rx="5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"></rect><path d="M13 5 v9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"></path><path d="M9.5 14 L13 19 L16.5 14 Z" fill="var(--signal)"></path><path d="M5 20.5 h16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-dasharray="2 2.4"></path></svg>ProtocolProbe</a><nav aria-label="Main" class="ml-auto hidden gap-5 text-sm text-ink-2 md:flex"><a href="/mcp/servers" class="no-underline hover:text-ink">Servers</a><a href="/mcp/reports" class="no-underline hover:text-ink">Reports</a><a href="/operators" class="no-underline hover:text-ink">Operators</a></nav><label class="theme-toggle max-md:ml-auto md:order-2"><input type="checkbox" id="theme-flip" aria-label="Switch between light and dark theme"/><span aria-hidden="true">◐</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="hidden sm:inline">theme</span></label><nav aria-label="Main (compact)" class="flex gap-3 text-sm text-ink-2 md:hidden"><a href="/mcp/servers" class="no-underline">Servers</a><a href="/operators" class="hidden no-underline min-[412px]:inline">Operators</a><a href="/mcp/reports" class="hidden no-underline min-[480px]:inline">Reports</a></nav><details class="explore md:order-1"><summary class="text-sm text-ink-2 hover:text-ink">Explore</summary><nav aria-label="Explore everything" class="explore-panel"><section aria-labelledby="explore-choose" class="min-w-0"><p id="explore-choose" class="eyebrow">Choose a server</p><p class="mt-1 text-[13px] text-ink-3">Find, filter, rank and compare registry servers.</p><ul class="mt-2 grid gap-1.5"><li><a href="/mcp/servers/search" class="link text-[14px]">Search by name or description</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/tools" class="link text-[14px]">Search MCP tools by name</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/page/1#filters" class="link text-[14px]">Browse and filter every server</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/tested/1" class="link text-[14px]">Servers we opened live (read-only)</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/top" class="link text-[14px]">Rankings: downloads, stars, record checks</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/compared" class="link text-[14px]">Most downloaded and starred, compared by topic</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/compare" class="link text-[14px]">Compare two servers</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/same-tools" class="link text-[14px]">Servers with the same tools</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/publishers" class="link text-[14px]">Servers by publisher</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/tool-type/changes-data/1" class="link text-[14px]">Servers whose tools change data</a></li></ul></section><section aria-labelledby="explore-yours" class="min-w-0"><p id="explore-yours" class="eyebrow">Test your own server</p><p class="mt-1 text-[13px] text-ink-3">Run our checks from your machine; nothing is sent to us.</p><ul class="mt-2 grid gap-1.5"><li><a href="/docs/selftest" class="link text-[14px]">Self-test command</a></li><li><a href="/docs/selftest#url" class="link text-[14px]">Test your server at its URL</a></li><li><a href="/docs/selftest#credential" class="link text-[14px]">A server that needs a token</a></li><li><a href="/docs/selftest#ci" class="link text-[14px]">Run it in CI (GitHub code scanning)</a></li><li><a href="/docs/record-checks" class="link text-[14px]">How record checks are counted</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/search" class="link text-[14px]">Your server’s page and README badge</a></li><li><a href="/docs/discover" class="link text-[14px]">Discover servers on your machine</a></li></ul></section><section aria-labelledby="explore-data" class="min-w-0"><p id="explore-data" class="eyebrow">Use the data</p><p class="mt-1 text-[13px] text-ink-3">Free to reuse, with dates and sources.</p><ul class="mt-2 grid gap-1.5"><li><a href="/docs/api" class="link text-[14px]">API (no key)</a></li><li><a href="/docs/cite" class="link text-[14px]">Dataset and how to cite</a></li><li><a href="/feed.xml" class="link text-[14px]">Feed: reports, updates, corrections</a></li><li><a href="/llms.txt" class="link text-[14px]">llms.txt for AI tools</a></li></ul></section><section aria-labelledby="explore-understand" class="min-w-0"><p id="explore-understand" class="eyebrow">Understand the registry</p><p class="mt-1 text-[13px] text-ink-3">What we measured, how, and what changed.</p><ul class="mt-2 grid gap-1.5"><li><a href="/mcp/numbers" class="link text-[14px]">MCP in numbers: every figure, with charts</a></li><li><a href="/updates/three-models" class="link text-[14px]">Tool lists at three AI models</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/reports/registry-vs-reality" class="link text-[14px]">Main report</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/reports/catalogue" class="link text-[14px]">What is in the registry</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/reports/not-tested" class="link text-[14px]">Why some servers are not tested</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/changes" class="link text-[14px]">Changes: registry and re-checked facts</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/removed" class="link text-[14px]">Servers removed from the registry</a></li><li><a href="/methodology" class="link text-[14px]">Methodology</a></li><li><a href="/updates" class="link text-[14px]">Updates</a></li><li><a href="/corrections" class="link text-[14px]">Corrections log</a></li></ul></section></nav></details></div></header><main id="main" class="wrap"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/servers/dev.modelmarket/mcp-security#page","url":"https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/servers/dev.modelmarket/mcp-security","name":"dev.modelmarket/mcp-security — MCP server record","description":"dev.modelmarket/mcp-security 1.0.0: “Scan MCP tool definitions for poisoning, look up server history, count tool-list tokens. Free” (publisher's words). MCP server by modelmarket.dev. 5 of 5 record checks met (not a safety rating).","dateModified":"2026-10-23","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://protocolprobe.com/#site"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://protocolprobe.com/#org"},"about":{"@id":"https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/servers/dev.modelmarket/mcp-security#software"}},{"@type":"SoftwareSourceCode","@id":"https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/servers/dev.modelmarket/mcp-security#software","name":"dev.modelmarket/mcp-security","subjectOf":{"@id":"https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/servers/dev.modelmarket/mcp-security#page"},"version":"1.0.0","description":"Scan MCP tool definitions for poisoning, look up server history, count tool-list tokens. Free.","programmingLanguage":"TypeScript","codeRepository":"https://github.com/alexar76/warden"},{"@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/servers/dev.modelmarket/mcp-security#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/servers/dev.modelmarket/mcp-security#page"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Who publishes dev.modelmarket/mcp-security?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The registry ties the namespace dev.modelmarket to the domain modelmarket.dev; only its owner can publish under it. Its linked repository is github.com/alexar76/warden; GitHub reports its owner as alexar76, a personal account. These are facts from the registry and GitHub, not a rating."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is dev.modelmarket/mcp-security safe to install?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We do not rate servers as safe or unsafe. 5 of its 5 applicable record checks are met (facts from public records, each listed on this page). What the records show: Its source repository opens publicly. Its repository had a push in the last 90 days. 1 of its tools describes changing data (our AI model's reading of the descriptions). These are facts with their sources on this page, not a safety guarantee, and we did not run its tools."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is dev.modelmarket/mcp-security free to use?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Its website (modelmarket.dev/tools/) describes a free pricing model. This is an AI-classified reading of the page on 2026-10-23, so check the page itself before relying on it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does dev.modelmarket/mcp-security need an API key or sign-in?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It opened a session without any credential on 2026-10-23. The registry entry declares no required credential; no declaration is not a guarantee."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Has dev.modelmarket/mcp-security been security tested?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Partly. 2 of the 14 checks that apply to it were exercised. We connected and read what the server declares, but did not call its tools: ProtocolProbe calls no server's tools for anything it publishes. This is our choice, not a block by the server. No security verdict is published before verification."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What can dev.modelmarket/mcp-security do?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It lists 4 tools. In our AI model's reading of their descriptions (two runs had to agree, nobody checked it by hand), they include tools that read or search and move money. We did not call any tool, so this describes the text, not the behaviour."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can dev.modelmarket/mcp-security change or delete data?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"1 of its tools says in its description that it creates, edits, deletes, sends or runs something (our AI model's reading). We did not call any tool, so we cannot say what actually happens."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does dev.modelmarket/mcp-security publish a security policy?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes: its repository has a public security policy (github.com/alexar76/warden/blob/HEAD/SECURITY.md). That is the publisher's statement, not permission for us to test the server, and we call none of its tools."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is the source code of dev.modelmarket/mcp-security?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In github.com/alexar76/warden, which opens publicly."}}]},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","@id":"https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/servers/dev.modelmarket/mcp-security#breadcrumb","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"MCP servers","item":"https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/servers"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"dev.modelmarket","item":"https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/publishers/dev.modelmarket"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"mcp-security"}]}]}</script><div class="sp-hero"><p class="sp-crumbs"><a href="/mcp/servers">MCP servers</a> › <a href="/mcp/publishers/dev.modelmarket" title="All 4 servers from this publisher">dev.modelmarket</a> › <!-- -->mcp-security</p><p class="eyebrow mt-3">MCP server · registry snapshot <!-- -->2026-10-23<!-- --> · last tested 2026-10-23</p><h1 class="sp-title">dev.modelmarket/mcp-security</h1><p class="sp-ptitle"><span data-pub="">MCP security checks — WARDEN and HISTOR</span> <span class="src">— the publisher&#x27;s title</span></p><p class="sp-by"><span>by <b>modelmarket.dev</b> · <!-- -->domain<!-- --> <a class="src link" href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/registry/about#verifying-server-authenticity" rel="noopener" title="The registry ties a namespace to a GitHub account or a domain; only its owner can publish under it">(the registry&#x27;s namespace rule)</a></span><span>repository owner on GitHub: alexar76 (personal account)</span><span><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/warden" rel="nofollow noopener ugc" class="link">Source<!-- --> ↗</a></span><span><a href="https://modelmarket.dev/tools/" rel="nofollow noopener ugc" class="link">Website<!-- --> ↗</a></span></p><p class="sp-sub"><span data-pub="">Scan MCP tool definitions for poisoning, look up server history, count tool-list tokens. Free.</span> <span class="src">— the publisher&#x27;s description</span></p><div class="sp-chips"><a class="sp-chip sp-chip-rc" href="#record-checks" title="Facts read from public records only. No tool was called. Not a safety rating.">5 of 5 record checks met</a><span class="sp-chip sp-chip-ro" title="We opened a read-only session and read the tools it declares. No tool was called. Not a security rating.">Read-only · tools listed <!-- -->2026-10-23</span><span class="sp-chip ai">Topic: <!-- -->security<!-- --> · AI-classified</span><span class="sp-chip ai">Pricing: <!-- -->free<!-- --> · AI-classified</span><span class="sp-chip">version <!-- -->1.0.0</span><span class="sp-chip">TypeScript</span><span class="sp-chip">streamable HTTP</span><span class="sp-chip">4<!-- --> tools</span></div></div><nav class="sp-jump" aria-label="Jump to a section"><a href="#summary">Summary</a><a href="#offers">What it offers</a><a href="#tool-quality">Tool descriptions</a><a href="#setup">Add to your client</a><a href="#install">Install and updates</a><a href="#listing">Listing vs reality</a><a href="#maker">Who made it</a><a href="#llm-checks">Three models read the list</a><a href="#record-checks">Record checks</a><a href="#safe">Is it safe to install?</a><a href="#questions">Common questions</a><a href="#similar">Similar servers</a><a href="#reactions">React</a><a href="#tests">What we tested</a><a href="#timeline">What happened</a><a href="#classification">Classification</a><a href="#cite">Cite or correct</a></nav><section id="summary" aria-label="Summary" class="sp-panel sp-answer"><div><h2 class="sp-label">Summary</h2><p class="sp-lead">dev.modelmarket/mcp-security is a remote MCP server listed in the official MCP registry at version 1.0.0, under the namespace of the domain modelmarket.dev. Its linked repository is github.com/alexar76/warden; GitHub reports its owner as alexar76, a personal account. On 2026-10-23 ProtocolProbe connected to it in read-only mode and read its inventory: 4 tools, 0 resources and 0 prompts.</p><h3 class="sp-label mt-5">Record checks</h3><p class="sp-rc-count mt-1"><a href="#record-checks" class="no-underline text-ink">5 of 5 record checks met</a><span class="text-ink-3 text-[14px] font-normal"> · <!-- -->4 do not apply</span></p><ul class="sp-rc-mini" aria-label="Record checks"><li class="rc-met"><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">met<!-- -->: </span>Registry entry is active and says how to run it</li><li class="rc-met"><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">met<!-- -->: </span>Source repository link opens</li><li class="rc-met"><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">met<!-- -->: </span>Repository is not archived</li><li class="rc-met"><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">met<!-- -->: </span>Code pushed to the repository in the 90 days before our check</li><li class="rc-met"><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">met<!-- -->: </span>Repository publishes a security policy (SECURITY.md)</li><li class="rc-not-applicable"><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true">–</span><span class="sr-only">not applicable<!-- -->: </span>Package names its licence with a standard (SPDX) identifier</li><li class="rc-not-applicable"><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true">–</span><span class="sr-only">not applicable<!-- -->: </span>The version the registry lists can be installed and is not withdrawn</li><li class="rc-not-applicable"><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true">–</span><span class="sr-only">not applicable<!-- -->: </span>npm package carries build provenance (attestation)</li><li class="rc-not-applicable"><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true">–</span><span class="sr-only">not applicable<!-- -->: </span>No known critical or high advisory in the package or its dependencies</li></ul><ul class="sp-ranks"><li>Not ranked by downloads: a remote server publishes no download figure</li><li>Not ranked by stars: 0 stars (ranked from 10)</li></ul><p class="sp-note">From public records, not a safety rating. <a class="link" href="#record-checks">Each check with its reason</a> · <a class="link" href="#safe">Is it safe to install?</a></p><p id="operator" class="sp-note"><a class="link" href="/operators">Operate this server?</a> <a class="link" href="#cite">Correct a fact</a> · <a class="link" href="#cite">README badge</a> · <a class="link" href="/docs/selftest">Run the checks yourself</a></p></div><div><h2 class="sp-label">Key facts</h2><dl class="sp-kv"><div class="contents"><dt>Runs</dt><dd>remote (hosted by the publisher)</dd></div><div class="contents"><dt>Transport</dt><dd>streamable HTTP</dd></div><div class="contents"><dt>Your own values</dt><dd>none declared (not a guarantee)</dd></div><div class="contents"><dt>Sign-in</dt><dd>none needed to open a session</dd></div><div class="contents"><dt>Repository</dt><dd>public</dd></div><div class="contents"><dt>Tools</dt><dd>4</dd></div><div class="contents"><dt>Described as changing data</dt><dd>1 of 4 tools<span class="sp-ai">AI-classified</span></dd></div><div class="contents"><dt>Topic</dt><dd>security<span class="sp-ai">AI-classified</span></dd></div><div class="contents"><dt>Pricing</dt><dd>free<span class="sp-ai">AI-classified</span></dd></div><div class="contents"><dt>Last tested</dt><dd>2026-10-23</dd></div></dl><div id="token-cost" class="mt-5"><h3 class="sp-label">Tool list size</h3><p class="mt-1">1,257 tokens on Claude Opus 5.5</p><p class="sp-note">Added to every request that loads this server&#x27;s tools (4 tools). Counted with Anthropic&#x27;s token counter on 2026-10-24, from the tool list we read on 2026-10-23.<!-- --> Median across 23,424 counted servers: 2,725 tokens.<!-- --> <a class="link" href="/methodology#token-cost">How it is counted</a></p></div><div id="auth-kind" class="mt-5"><h3 class="sp-label">How a client gets in</h3><p class="mt-1">Connects without signing in</p><p class="sp-note">Read from the server&#x27;s public metadata on 2026-10-23 (modelmarket.dev), in our read-only connection; no tool was called. It may have changed since.<!-- --> <a class="link" href="/methodology#auth-kind">How it is read</a></p></div><div id="three-apis" class="mt-5"><h3 class="sp-label">Tool list at the three APIs</h3><div class="sp-apis"><details class="sp-api"><summary>Anthropic<!-- -->&#x27;s API · <!-- -->accepted</summary><div class="sp-api-body"><p><b>Claude Haiku 5.5</b></p><p>Claude Haiku 5.5 (Anthropic&#x27;s count): 1,330 prompt tokens for this tool list and the one-line request, on 2026-10-25. Counts from different vendors are not comparable.</p><p>Anthropic&#x27;s API accepted this list.</p><p>Claude Haiku 5.5 made no tool call; it answered without calling one.</p><p>Model version reported by the API: claude-haiku-5-5. Checked on 2026-10-25, from the tool list we read on 2026-10-23.</p></div></details><details class="sp-api"><summary>OpenAI<!-- -->&#x27;s API · <!-- -->accepted</summary><div class="sp-api-body"><p><b>GPT-5-nano</b></p><p>GPT-5-nano (OpenAI&#x27;s count): 640 prompt tokens for this tool list and the one-line request, on 2026-10-25. Counts from different vendors are not comparable.</p><p>OpenAI&#x27;s API accepted this list.</p><p>Tool chosen: warden_scan</p><p>The input was valid against the schema keywords we check.</p><p>Model version reported by the API: gpt-5-nano-2025-08-07. Checked on 2026-10-25, from the tool list we read on 2026-10-23.</p></div></details><details class="sp-api"><summary>Google<!-- -->&#x27;s API · <!-- -->accepted</summary><div class="sp-api-body"><p><b>Gemini 2.5 Flash</b></p><p>Gemini 2.5 Flash (Google&#x27;s count): 716 prompt tokens for this tool list and the one-line request, on 2026-10-26. Counts from different vendors are not comparable.</p><p>Google&#x27;s API accepted this list.</p><p>Gemini 2.5 Flash made no tool call; it answered without calling one.</p><p>Google&#x27;s API reported the call as malformed (MALFORMED_FUNCTION_CALL).</p><p>Model version reported by the API: gemini-2.5-flash. Checked on 2026-10-26, from the tool list we read on 2026-10-23.</p></div></details></div><p class="sp-note">One small model per API, on the date shown: not a ranking of the models and not a judgment of the server. A refusal is that API&#x27;s rule about the list as listed. <a class="link" href="#llm-checks">All results</a></p></div><p class="mt-5"><a href="#setup" class="btn">Add to your client</a></p></div></section><div class="sp-two"><div class="sp-panel"><h2 class="sp-label">Worth knowing before you connect it</h2><ul class="sp-know"><li class="t-attention">1 tool is described as changing something (x402_check): our AI model&#x27;s reading of the descriptions, not something we tested, and the server opened a session without any credential. We did not call it.</li></ul><p class="sp-note">Each line comes from a section below, with its source and date.</p></div><div class="sp-panel"><h2 class="sp-label">How fresh this is</h2><dl class="sp-kv"><dt>Live-tested</dt><dd>yes, a real session (not a text-only review)</dd><dt>Last tested</dt><dd>2026-10-23</dd><dt>Mode</dt><dd>read-only (no tool calls)</dd><dt>Latest version</dt><dd>1.0.0<!-- -->, published 2026-10-20<!-- --> <span class="src">(registry, as of the <!-- -->2026-10-23<!-- --> snapshot)</span></dd><dt>First listed version</dt><dd>2026-10-20<!-- --> <span class="src">(earliest version still in the registry; older removed versions would be earlier)</span></dd><dt>Registry data</dt><dd>snapshot <!-- -->2026-10-23</dd><dt>Package and repository</dt><dd>checked <!-- -->2026-10-22</dd><dt>Engine</dt><dd class="font-mono text-xs">mcp-runtime-engine@0.1.0<!-- --> · sdk@1.32.0</dd></dl><div id="stale" class="mt-5"><h3 class="sp-label">Dead or stale signals</h3><p class="mt-1 text-sm">None found in the records we hold</p><p class="sp-note">Looked for and not found: deprecated in the registry; repository link does not open; repository archived; no push in over 365 days. Does not apply: listed version cannot be installed or is withdrawn. Each line is a dated fact from a public record. It does not say whether the server still works, and a record can change after the date shown.</p></div></div></div><div class="sp-observed sp-changes" id="changes"><p class="sp-label">Changes since the last refresh</p><p>New in the registry: not in the list of 2026-10-04, listed on 2026-10-23 with version 1.0.0 (published 2026-10-20).</p><p class="sp-note">Source: the official MCP Registry list on 2026-10-04 and on 2026-10-23.</p></div><div class="sp-body"><nav class="sp-rail" aria-label="On this page"><span class="contents"><a href="#summary">Summary</a></span><span class="contents"><span class="grp">What it is</span><a href="#offers">What it offers</a></span><span class="contents"><a href="#tool-quality">Tool descriptions</a></span><span class="contents"><a href="#setup">Add to your client</a></span><span class="contents"><a href="#install">Install and updates</a></span><span class="contents"><a href="#listing">Listing vs reality</a></span><span class="contents"><a href="#maker">Who made it</a></span><span class="contents"><a href="#llm-checks">Three models read the list</a></span><span class="contents"><span class="grp">Choosing</span><a href="#record-checks">Record checks</a></span><span class="contents"><a href="#safe">Is it safe to install?</a></span><span class="contents"><a href="#questions">Common questions</a></span><span class="contents"><a href="#similar">Similar servers</a></span><span class="contents"><a href="#reactions">React</a></span><span class="contents"><span class="grp">Security testing</span><a href="#tests">What we tested</a></span><span class="contents"><a href="#timeline">What happened</a></span><span class="contents"><span class="grp">Reference</span><a href="#classification">Classification</a></span><span class="contents"><a href="#cite">Cite or correct</a></span></nav><div class="sp-content"><p class="sp-part">What it is</p><section id="offers" class="sp-sec" aria-labelledby="offers-h"><div class="sp-head" id="offers-h"><h2 class="sp-q">What does this server offer?</h2><span class="sp-label">Observed inventory</span></div><div class="sp-counts"><div class="sp-panel sp-count"><b>4</b><span>tools</span></div><div class="sp-panel sp-count"><b>0</b><span>resources</span></div><div class="sp-panel sp-count"><b>0</b><span>prompts</span></div></div><p class="sp-intro">1 of 4 tools are described as changing something (creating, editing, deleting, sending or running).</p><ul class="sp-toolist" aria-label="Tools and their descriptions"><li class="sp-tool"><div class="sp-tool-head"><span class="sp-tool-name" data-pub="">warden_scan</span><span class="sp-chip" title="AI reading of the description: returns, lists, searches or looks up information without changing anything">reads or searches</span></div><p class="sp-tool-desc" data-pub="">“<!-- -->Scan an MCP server&#x27;s tools/list with WARDEN, the open-source MCP firewall: static rules and a threat list over every name, description, schema and annotation.<!-- -->”</p><p class="sp-tool-hints">Publisher declares: <!-- -->read-only yes · destructive no · idempotent yes · open-world yes</p><details class="sp-params"><summary>2<!-- --> <!-- -->inputs<!-- -->, 1 required</summary><ul><li><code data-pub="">tools</code><span class="ty">array</span><span class="rq">required</span><span class="ds" data-pub="">“<!-- -->The server&#x27;s tools/list result: [{name, description, inputSchema, ...}]<!-- -->”</span></li><li><code data-pub="">server</code><span class="ty">object</span><span class="ds" data-pub="">“<!-- -->Optional {name, url} to label the verdict<!-- -->”</span></li></ul></details></li><li class="sp-tool"><div class="sp-tool-head"><span class="sp-tool-name" data-pub="">histor_check</span><span class="sp-chip" title="AI reading of the description: returns, lists, searches or looks up information without changing anything">reads or searches</span></div><p class="sp-tool-desc" data-pub="">“<!-- -->Look up an MCP server in HISTOR, a public append-only log of MCP tool sets: when its tool set was first pinned, how often it changed, and what the pattern scan found.<!-- -->”</p><p class="sp-tool-hints">Publisher declares: <!-- -->read-only yes · destructive no · idempotent yes · open-world yes</p><details class="sp-params"><summary>2<!-- --> <!-- -->inputs</summary><ul><li><code data-pub="">endpoint</code><span class="ty">string</span><span class="ds" data-pub="">“<!-- -->https URL of the MCP server<!-- -->”</span></li><li><code data-pub="">name</code><span class="ty">string</span><span class="ds" data-pub="">“<!-- -->Or its registry name, e.g.<!-- -->”</span></li></ul></details></li><li class="sp-tool"><div class="sp-tool-head"><span class="sp-tool-name" data-pub="">tool_list_cost</span><span class="sp-chip" title="AI reading of the description: returns, lists, searches or looks up information without changing anything">reads or searches</span></div><p class="sp-tool-desc" data-pub="">“<!-- -->How many tokens an MCP server&#x27;s tool list adds to every model request, what that costs per 1,000 requests, the heaviest tools, and where it sits among 18,204 packages and 16,170 remote servers.<!-- -->”</p><p class="sp-tool-hints">Publisher declares: <!-- -->read-only yes · destructive no · idempotent yes · open-world yes</p><details class="sp-params"><summary>2<!-- --> <!-- -->inputs</summary><ul><li><code data-pub="">tools</code><span class="ty">array</span><span class="ds" data-pub="">“<!-- -->A tools/list result<!-- -->”</span></li><li><code data-pub="">server</code><span class="ty">string</span><span class="ds" data-pub="">“<!-- -->Or a server HISTOR observes: https endpoint, npm:&lt;package&gt;, pypi:&lt;package&gt; or registry name<!-- -->”</span></li></ul></details></li><li class="sp-tool w"><div class="sp-tool-head"><span class="sp-tool-name" data-pub="">x402_check</span><a class="sp-tool-shared" href="/mcp/tools?q=x402_check">on <!-- -->10<!-- --> other server<!-- -->s</a><span class="sp-chip" title="AI reading of the description: pays, charges, trades, places orders or refunds">moves money</span><span class="sp-chip sp-chip-w">described as changing data</span></div><p class="sp-tool-desc" data-pub="">“<!-- -->Check a signed x402 USDC payment before submitting it: recovers the EIP-712 signer, runs USDC&#x27;s own checks and the seller&#x27;s terms, and when the signature fails names the domain it was really made for…<!-- -->”</p><p class="sp-tool-hints">Publisher declares: <!-- -->read-only yes · destructive no · idempotent yes · open-world yes</p><details class="sp-params"><summary>5<!-- --> <!-- -->inputs</summary><ul><li><code data-pub="">x_payment</code><span class="ty">string</span><span class="ds" data-pub="">“<!-- -->The X-PAYMENT header (base64)<!-- -->”</span></li><li><code data-pub="">requirements</code><span class="ty">object</span><span class="ds" data-pub="">“<!-- -->The 402&#x27;s accepts entry: payTo, amount, asset, network<!-- -->”</span></li><li><code data-pub="">authorization</code><span class="ty">object</span><span class="ds" data-pub="">“<!-- -->Instead of x_payment: from, to, value, validAfter, validBefore, nonce<!-- -->”</span></li><li><code data-pub="">signature</code><span class="ty">string</span><span class="ds" data-pub="">“<!-- -->With authorization: the 65-byte hex signature<!-- -->”</span></li><li><code data-pub="">network</code><span class="ty">string</span><span class="ds" data-pub="">“<!-- -->With authorization: base, base-sepolia, … or eip155:&lt;id&gt;<!-- -->”</span></li></ul></details></li></ul><p class="sp-note">Each quoted sentence is the first sentence of the publisher’s own description. The kind of tool and the “changes data” mark are our AI model’s reading of that description, not something we tested: two differently worded runs had to agree, otherwise no label is shown, and nobody has checked them by hand. A tool without the “changes data” mark is described as only reading, searching or calculating, or the two runs did not agree. No tool was called. Read the publisher’s full description before relying on it.<!-- --> “Publisher declares” lists the hints the server itself sends with the tool (MCP annotations: read-only, destructive, idempotent, open-world); they are the publisher&#x27;s claims, not checked by us.<!-- --> Inputs are the parameters in the tool&#x27;s own input schema: name, declared type, whether it is required, and the first sentence of its description.<!-- --> Read 2026-10-23.</p></section><section id="tool-quality" class="sp-sec" aria-labelledby="tool-quality-h"><details class="sp-fold" open=""><summary class="sp-head" id="tool-quality-h"><h2 class="sp-q">How well are its tools described?</h2><span class="sp-label">Features #4 and #5</span></summary><p class="sp-intro">How clearly this server&#x27;s own tool descriptions say what a tool does, and how consistent its tool list is. The first part is an AI model&#x27;s yes/no reading of each description; the second part is counted. We do not turn it into a grade.</p><div class="sp-grid"><div class="sp-panel"><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold">Descriptions</h3><p class="sp-label mt-3">AI reading of each description</p><dl class="sp-kv"><div class="contents"><dt>Says what the tool does</dt><dd>100%<!-- --> <span class="text-ink-3">of <!-- -->4<!-- --> <!-- -->tools</span></dd></div><div class="contents"><dt>Says what it returns</dt><dd>100%<!-- --> <span class="text-ink-3">of <!-- -->4<!-- --> <!-- -->tools</span></dd></div><div class="contents"><dt>States limits, defaults or errors</dt><dd>0%<!-- --> <span class="text-ink-3">of <!-- -->3<!-- --> <!-- -->tools</span></dd></div><div class="contents"><dt>Says when to use it</dt><dd>100%<!-- --> <span class="text-ink-3">of <!-- -->4<!-- --> <!-- -->tools</span></dd></div><dt>Items covered per tool</dt><dd>3.3<!-- --> of 4 on average</dd></dl><p class="sp-label mt-4">Counted from the listing</p><dl class="sp-kv"><dt>Parameters with a description</dt><dd>100%<!-- --> <span class="text-ink-3">of <!-- -->11</span></dd><dt>Tools with a description</dt><dd>100%<!-- --> <span class="text-ink-3">of <!-- -->4</span></dd><dt>Typical description length</dt><dd>261<!-- --> characters</dd></dl></div><div class="sp-panel"><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold">The tool set</h3><p class="sp-label mt-3">Counted from the listing</p><dl class="sp-kv"><dt>Tools</dt><dd>4</dd><dt>Size of the list</dt><dd>about <!-- -->800<!-- --> tokens for an agent to load <span class="text-ink-3">(characters ÷ 4)</span></dd><dt>Naming</dt><dd>4<!-- --> of <!-- -->4<!-- --> names use <!-- -->snake_case</dd></dl><p class="sp-label mt-4">AI reading: easy to mix up</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm">No pair found.</p></div></div><p class="sp-note">The AI items cover <!-- -->4<!-- --> of <!-- -->4<!-- --> tools: for a tool where two differently worded runs disagreed, that item is left out. They were not checked by hand, and no tool was called. “Easy to mix up” means two tools whose names or descriptions overlap without saying how they differ; the AI found <!-- -->none<!-- -->. We do not rate whether the tool set is complete or whether side effects are spelled out, because our AI reading of those was not reliable enough.</p></details></section><section id="setup" class="sp-sec" aria-labelledby="setup-h"><details class="sp-fold" open=""><summary class="sp-head" id="setup-h"><h2 class="sp-q">How do I add it to my client?</h2><span class="sp-label">Config from the registry entry</span></summary><div class="sp-setup"><h3 class="h4">From the remote endpoint (Streamable HTTP)</h3><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-2">We connected to this URL on 2026-10-23<!-- --> (a read-only session: no tool was called).</p><p class="sp-oneclick"><a class="btn" href="cursor://anysphere.cursor-deeplink/mcp/install?name=mcp-security&amp;config=eyJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL21vZGVsbWFya2V0LmRldi90b29scy9tY3Avc2VjdXJpdHkifQ%3D%3D">Add to Cursor</a><span class="sp-note">An install link in the format Cursor documents, holding the Cursor config below.</span></p><details class="sp-snip" open=""><summary>Claude Desktop or claude.ai</summary><pre class="sp-pre sp-code">Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector, then paste:
https://modelmarket.dev/tools/mcp/security</pre></details><details class="sp-snip"><summary>Cursor<span class="src"> · <!-- -->.cursor/mcp.json in a project, or ~/.cursor/mcp.json</span></summary><pre class="sp-pre sp-code">{
  &quot;mcpServers&quot;: {
    &quot;mcp-security&quot;: {
      &quot;url&quot;: &quot;https://modelmarket.dev/tools/mcp/security&quot;
    }
  }
}</pre></details><details class="sp-snip"><summary>VS Code<span class="src"> · <!-- -->.vscode/mcp.json</span></summary><pre class="sp-pre sp-code">{
  &quot;servers&quot;: {
    &quot;mcp-security&quot;: {
      &quot;type&quot;: &quot;http&quot;,
      &quot;url&quot;: &quot;https://modelmarket.dev/tools/mcp/security&quot;
    }
  }
}</pre></details><details class="sp-snip"><summary>VS Code (command line)<span class="src"> · <!-- -->Bash or zsh terminal (macOS, Linux)</span></summary><pre class="sp-pre sp-code">code --add-mcp &#x27;{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;mcp-security&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;http&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://modelmarket.dev/tools/mcp/security&quot;}&#x27;</pre></details><details class="sp-snip"><summary>Claude Code</summary><pre class="sp-pre sp-code">claude mcp add --transport http mcp-security https://modelmarket.dev/tools/mcp/security</pre></details><details class="sp-snip"><summary>Cline<span class="src"> · <!-- -->cline_mcp_settings.json (Cline CLI: ~/.cline/data/settings/; in the editor: MCP Servers → Configure → Configure MCP Servers)</span></summary><pre class="sp-pre sp-code">{
  &quot;mcpServers&quot;: {
    &quot;mcp-security&quot;: {
      &quot;type&quot;: &quot;streamableHttp&quot;,
      &quot;url&quot;: &quot;https://modelmarket.dev/tools/mcp/security&quot;,
      &quot;disabled&quot;: false,
      &quot;autoApprove&quot;: []
    }
  }
}</pre></details><details class="sp-snip"><summary>Gemini CLI<span class="src"> · <!-- -->~/.gemini/settings.json, or .gemini/settings.json in a project</span></summary><pre class="sp-pre sp-code">{
  &quot;mcpServers&quot;: {
    &quot;mcp-security&quot;: {
      &quot;httpUrl&quot;: &quot;https://modelmarket.dev/tools/mcp/security&quot;
    }
  }
}</pre></details><details class="sp-snip"><summary>OpenAI Codex<span class="src"> · <!-- -->~/.codex/config.toml, or .codex/config.toml in a trusted project</span></summary><pre class="sp-pre sp-code">[mcp_servers.mcp-security]
url = &quot;https://modelmarket.dev/tools/mcp/security&quot;</pre></details><details class="sp-snip"><summary>Zed<span class="src"> · <!-- -->Zed settings file (command: zed: open settings file)</span></summary><pre class="sp-pre sp-code">{
  &quot;context_servers&quot;: {
    &quot;mcp-security&quot;: {
      &quot;url&quot;: &quot;https://modelmarket.dev/tools/mcp/security&quot;
    }
  }
}</pre></details><details class="sp-snip"><summary>Try it in the MCP Inspector<span class="src"> · <!-- -->runs on your machine, opens in your browser · Node 22.19+</span></summary><pre class="sp-pre sp-code">npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector@2.11.0 --server-url https://modelmarket.dev/tools/mcp/security --transport http</pre></details><ul class="sp-notes mt-2"><li>The server runs on the operator&#x27;s infrastructure; it may ask you to sign in when you first connect.</li><li>Zed&#x27;s docs we read on 2026-10-26 describe remote servers by URL and do not name the transport.</li><li>The MCP Inspector lists the server&#x27;s tools, resources and prompts; a tool you call there runs for real.</li></ul></div><p class="sp-note">Built from the server&#x27;s registry entry with each client&#x27;s documented format (checked 2026-10-14; the Cursor link and the VS Code command 2026-10-19; the MCP Inspector command 2026-10-21; Cline, Gemini CLI, OpenAI Codex and Zed 2026-10-26). Values in &lt; &gt; are yours to fill in; this page never contains a key. Where the server needs a setting the entry does not declare, it can still fail to start.</p></details></section><section id="listing" class="sp-sec" aria-labelledby="listing-h"><div class="sp-head" id="listing-h"><h2 class="sp-q">Does the registry listing match what we found?</h2><span class="sp-label">Feature #6</span></div><p class="sp-intro">The registry checks an entry when it is published (each new version), and nothing re-checks it on a schedule. A difference below is about the listing, not a judgement of the publisher.</p><div class="sp-panel sp-scroll"><table class="sp-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Registry says</th><th scope="col">We found</th><th scope="col">Result</th><th scope="col">Source · date</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Remote endpoint modelmarket.dev/tools/mcp/security</td><td>Session opened</td><td><span class="sp-res matches">matches</span></td><td>our test<!-- --> · 2026-10-23</td></tr><tr><td>No credential declared as required</td><td>Opened a session without any credential</td><td><span class="sp-res matches">matches</span></td><td>our test<!-- --> · 2026-10-23</td></tr><tr><td>Repository github.com/alexar76/warden</td><td>Opens publicly</td><td><span class="sp-res matches">matches</span></td><td>api.github.com<!-- --> · 2026-10-22</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section id="maker" class="sp-sec" aria-labelledby="maker-h"><details class="sp-fold" open=""><summary class="sp-head" id="maker-h"><h2 class="sp-q">Who made it?</h2><span class="sp-label">Feature #7 · lineage</span></summary><p class="sp-intro">Facts about the publisher. We do not turn them into a trust score.</p><div class="sp-grid"><div class="sp-panel"><dl class="sp-kv"><dt>Namespace</dt><dd class="font-mono"><a class="link" href="/mcp/publishers/dev.modelmarket">dev.modelmarket</a><span class="text-ink-3"> · <!-- -->4<!-- --> servers</span></dd><dt>GitHub owner</dt><dd>a personal account<!-- --> (alexar76)</dd></dl></div><div class="sp-panel"><dl class="sp-kv"><dt>Repository</dt><dd><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/warden" rel="nofollow noopener ugc" class="link">github.com/alexar76/warden</a></dd><dt>Stars</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Repository age</dt><dd>31–90 days</dd><dt>Last push</dt><dd>0–30 days<!-- --> ago</dd><dt>Archived</dt><dd>no</dd><dt>Security policy</dt><dd><a href="https://github.com/alexar76/warden/blob/HEAD/SECURITY.md" rel="nofollow noopener ugc" class="link">SECURITY.md</a></dd></dl></div></div><p class="sp-note">Source: the registry entry and api.github.com<!-- --> · 2026-10-22<!-- -->; security policy read from GitHub · 2026-10-23<!-- -->.</p><p class="sp-note">Publish this server? Run these checks against it yourself before release, from your own machine: a server the command starts, or your own server at its URL after a one-time proof that you control it: <a class="link" href="/docs/selftest"><code>npx protocolprobe-selftest</code></a>.</p></details></section><section id="llm-checks" class="sp-sec" aria-labelledby="llm-checks-h"><details class="sp-fold" open=""><summary class="sp-head" id="llm-checks-h"><h2 class="sp-q">How three small models read this tool list</h2><span class="sp-label">Tool list sent to three models · no tool called</span></summary><div class="sp-panel p-[18px_22px]"><p class="sp-note">Each list was sent once to three small, low-cost models, each at its lowest reasoning setting, with the same one-line request and no system prompt: Claude Haiku 5.5, GPT-5-nano and Gemini 2.5 Flash. These results describe that model on that day, not the vendor&#x27;s other models and not how a real client will behave; larger models, reasoning, or a client&#x27;s own system prompt can give different results.</p><div class="mt-3"><h4 class="text-[13px] font-semibold">Claude Haiku 5.5</h4><p class="text-sm">Claude Haiku 5.5 (Anthropic&#x27;s count): 1,330 prompt tokens for this tool list and the one-line request, on 2026-10-25. Counts from different vendors are not comparable.</p><ul class="text-sm"><li>Anthropic&#x27;s API accepted this list.</li><li>Claude Haiku 5.5 made no tool call; it answered without calling one.</li><li>Tool calls in the answer: 0.</li><li>Runs: 2 of 2. Both answers to the same request had a call that did not match the list or its schema, or no call; the second is shown.</li><li>Model version reported by the API: claude-haiku-5-5. Checked on 2026-10-25, from the tool list we read on 2026-10-23.</li></ul></div><div class="mt-3"><h4 class="text-[13px] font-semibold">GPT-5-nano</h4><p class="text-sm">GPT-5-nano (OpenAI&#x27;s count): 640 prompt tokens for this tool list and the one-line request, on 2026-10-25. Counts from different vendors are not comparable.</p><ul class="text-sm"><li>OpenAI&#x27;s API accepted this list.</li><li>Tool chosen: warden_scan</li><li>The input was valid against the schema keywords we check.</li><li>Tool calls in the answer: 1.</li><li>Runs: 1 of 1.</li><li>Model version reported by the API: gpt-5-nano-2025-08-07. Checked on 2026-10-25, from the tool list we read on 2026-10-23.</li></ul></div><div class="mt-3"><h4 class="text-[13px] font-semibold">Gemini 2.5 Flash</h4><p class="text-sm">Gemini 2.5 Flash (Google&#x27;s count): 716 prompt tokens for this tool list and the one-line request, on 2026-10-26. Counts from different vendors are not comparable.</p><ul class="text-sm"><li>Google&#x27;s API accepted this list.</li><li>Gemini 2.5 Flash made no tool call; it answered without calling one.</li><li>Google&#x27;s API reported the call as malformed (MALFORMED_FUNCTION_CALL).</li><li>Tool calls in the answer: 0.</li><li>Runs: 2 of 2. Both answers to the same request had a call that did not match the list or its schema, or no call; the second is shown.</li><li>Model version reported by the API: gemini-2.5-flash. Checked on 2026-10-26, from the tool list we read on 2026-10-23.</li></ul></div><p class="sp-note mt-2"><a class="link" href="/methodology#cross-llm">How the lists were sent and checked</a></p></div></details></section><p class="sp-part">Choosing</p><section id="record-checks" class="sp-sec" aria-labelledby="record-checks-h"><div class="sp-head" id="record-checks-h"><h2 class="sp-q">Record checks</h2><span class="sp-label">Public records · not a safety rating</span></div><div class="sp-panel p-[18px_22px]"><p class="sp-rc-count">5 of 5 record checks met<span class="text-ink-3"> · <!-- -->4 do not apply</span></p><ul class="sp-ranks"><li>Not ranked by downloads: a remote server publishes no download figure</li><li>Not ranked by stars: 0 stars (ranked from 10)</li></ul><ul class="sp-rc"><li class="rc-met"><span class="st">Met</span><span class="lb">Registry entry is active and says how to run it</span><span class="dt">Active, with a package or a remote address.</span></li><li class="rc-met"><span class="st">Met</span><span class="lb">Source repository link opens</span><span class="dt">The linked GitHub repository is public.</span></li><li class="rc-met"><span class="st">Met</span><span class="lb">Repository is not archived</span><span class="dt">Not archived.</span></li><li class="rc-met"><span class="st">Met</span><span class="lb">Code pushed to the repository in the 90 days before our check</span><span class="dt">Last push 0-30 days before our check.</span></li><li class="rc-met"><span class="st">Met</span><span class="lb">Repository publishes a security policy (SECURITY.md)</span><span class="dt">SECURITY.md found.</span></li><li class="rc-not-applicable"><span class="st">Does not apply</span><span class="lb">Package names its licence with a standard (SPDX) identifier</span><span class="dt">Remote server: it ships no package.</span></li><li class="rc-not-applicable"><span class="st">Does not apply</span><span class="lb">The version the registry lists can be installed and is not withdrawn</span><span class="dt">Remote server: it ships no package.</span></li><li class="rc-not-applicable"><span class="st">Does not apply</span><span class="lb">npm package carries build provenance (attestation)</span><span class="dt">Remote server: it ships no package.</span></li><li class="rc-not-applicable"><span class="st">Does not apply</span><span class="lb">No known critical or high advisory in the package or its dependencies</span><span class="dt">Remote server: it ships no package.</span></li></ul><p class="sp-note mt-3">Read from public records only: the registry entry, npm/PyPI, GitHub and advisory databases<!-- -->, checked 2026-10-22<!-- -->. No tool was called. Only “met” and “not met” are counted, so the total differs between servers; a check that does not apply or that we could not run is listed, never counted against it. It is not a safety rating. <a class="link" href="/docs/record-checks">How each check works</a> · <a class="link" href="/mcp/servers/top">Leaderboards</a></p></div></section><section id="questions" class="sp-sec" aria-labelledby="questions-h"><div class="sp-head" id="questions-h"><h2 class="sp-q">Common questions about dev.modelmarket/mcp-security</h2><span class="sp-label">Answered from the data above</span></div><div class="sp-panel sp-faq"><div id="publisher"><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold">Who publishes dev.modelmarket/mcp-security?</h3><p>The registry ties the namespace dev.modelmarket to the domain modelmarket.dev; only its owner can publish under it. Its linked repository is github.com/alexar76/warden; GitHub reports its owner as alexar76, a personal account. These are facts from the registry and GitHub, not a rating.</p></div><div id="safe"><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold">Is dev.modelmarket/mcp-security safe to install?</h3><p>We do not rate servers as safe or unsafe. 5 of its 5 applicable record checks are met (facts from public records, each listed on this page). What the records show: Its source repository opens publicly. Its repository had a push in the last 90 days. 1 of its tools describes changing data (our AI model&#x27;s reading of the descriptions). These are facts with their sources on this page, not a safety guarantee, and we did not run its tools.</p></div><div><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold">Is dev.modelmarket/mcp-security free to use?</h3><p>Its website (modelmarket.dev/tools/) describes a free pricing model. This is an AI-classified reading of the page on 2026-10-23, so check the page itself before relying on it.</p></div><div><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold">Does dev.modelmarket/mcp-security need an API key or sign-in?</h3><p>It opened a session without any credential on 2026-10-23. The registry entry declares no required credential; no declaration is not a guarantee.</p></div><div><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold">Has dev.modelmarket/mcp-security been security tested?</h3><p>Partly. 2 of the 14 checks that apply to it were exercised. We connected and read what the server declares, but did not call its tools: ProtocolProbe calls no server&#x27;s tools for anything it publishes. This is our choice, not a block by the server. No security verdict is published before verification.</p></div><div><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold">What can dev.modelmarket/mcp-security do?</h3><p>It lists 4 tools. In our AI model&#x27;s reading of their descriptions (two runs had to agree, nobody checked it by hand), they include tools that read or search and move money. We did not call any tool, so this describes the text, not the behaviour.</p></div><div><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold">Can dev.modelmarket/mcp-security change or delete data?</h3><p>1 of its tools says in its description that it creates, edits, deletes, sends or runs something (our AI model&#x27;s reading). We did not call any tool, so we cannot say what actually happens.</p></div><div><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold">Does dev.modelmarket/mcp-security publish a security policy?</h3><p>Yes: its repository has a public security policy (github.com/alexar76/warden/blob/HEAD/SECURITY.md). That is the publisher&#x27;s statement, not permission for us to test the server, and we call none of its tools.</p></div><div><h3 class="text-[15px] font-semibold">Where is the source code of dev.modelmarket/mcp-security?</h3><p>In github.com/alexar76/warden, which opens publicly.</p></div></div></section><section id="reactions" class="sp-sec" aria-labelledby="reactions-h"><div class="sp-head" id="reactions-h"><h2 class="sp-q">Found this page useful?</h2><span class="sp-label">Anonymous · no sign-in</span></div><div class="sp-panel p-[18px_22px]"><p class="text-sm text-ink-2">A quick, anonymous reaction — no account, no email. One per kind from your browser. The tally updates when the page is next refreshed, and it is only a rough count, never a safety rating or a measured number of people.</p><div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2.5"><form class="contents" action="/api/react" method="post"><input type="hidden" name="server" value="dev.modelmarket/mcp-security"/><input type="hidden" name="kind" value="like"/><button type="submit" class="btn inline-flex items-center gap-2" aria-label="Like this page"><span aria-hidden="true">👍</span><span>Like</span><span class="rounded-full bg-rule/60 px-2 text-[13px] tabular-nums text-ink-2" aria-label="0 so far">0</span></button></form><form class="contents" action="/api/react" method="post"><input type="hidden" name="server" value="dev.modelmarket/mcp-security"/><input type="hidden" name="kind" value="love"/><button type="submit" class="btn inline-flex items-center gap-2" aria-label="Love this page"><span aria-hidden="true">❤</span><span>Love</span><span class="rounded-full bg-rule/60 px-2 text-[13px] tabular-nums text-ink-2" aria-label="0 so far">0</span></button></form></div></div></section><section id="similar" class="sp-sec" aria-labelledby="similar-h"><details class="sp-fold" open=""><summary class="sp-head" id="similar-h"><h2 class="sp-q">Similar servers</h2><span class="sp-label">Same topic · AI-read</span></summary><ul class="sp-similar"><li><a class="nm" href="/mcp/servers/com.decionis/mcp">com.decionis/mcp</a><span class="mt"><span>also has tools that <!-- -->moves money, reads or searches</span><a href="/mcp/compare?a=dev.modelmarket/mcp-security&amp;b=com.decionis/mcp">compare with this one</a></span></li><li><a class="nm" href="/mcp/servers/io.github.JesseGdotIO/hermes-plant">io.github.JesseGdotIO/hermes-plant</a><span class="bl">Hermes Plant — Agent Commerce Assurance</span><span class="mt"><span>also has tools that <!-- -->moves money, reads or searches</span><a href="/mcp/compare?a=dev.modelmarket/mcp-security&amp;b=io.github.JesseGdotIO/hermes-plant">compare with this one</a></span></li><li><a class="nm" href="/mcp/servers/io.github.philpof102-svg/mainstreet">io.github.philpof102-svg/mainstreet</a><span class="mt"><span>also has tools that <!-- -->moves money, reads or searches</span><a href="/mcp/compare?a=dev.modelmarket/mcp-security&amp;b=io.github.philpof102-svg/mainstreet">compare with this one</a></span></li><li><a class="nm" href="/mcp/servers/com.decision-anchor/da">com.decision-anchor/da</a><span class="bl">Decision Anchor</span><span class="mt"><span>also has tools that <!-- -->moves money, reads or searches</span><a href="/mcp/compare?a=dev.modelmarket/mcp-security&amp;b=com.decision-anchor/da">compare with this one</a></span></li><li><a class="nm" href="/mcp/servers/com.fidacy/ai-agent-firewall">com.fidacy/ai-agent-firewall</a><span class="mt"><span>also has tools that <!-- -->moves money, reads or searches</span><a href="/mcp/compare?a=dev.modelmarket/mcp-security&amp;b=com.fidacy/ai-agent-firewall">compare with this one</a></span></li><li><a class="nm" href="/mcp/servers/com.kenwea.www/marketplace">com.kenwea.www/marketplace</a><span class="bl">Kenwea — Sandbox Attestation &amp; Agent Marketplace</span><span class="mt"><span>also has tools that <!-- -->moves money, reads or searches</span><a href="/mcp/compare?a=dev.modelmarket/mcp-security&amp;b=com.kenwea.www/marketplace">compare with this one</a></span></li></ul><p class="sp-note">Active servers whose topic is also “security” and that have at least one tool of the same kind; most kinds in common first, then most GitHub stars.<!-- --> <!-- -->The topic and the tool kinds are an AI model&#x27;s reading of the publishers&#x27; descriptions, not checked by hand. Similar is not a recommendation.</p></details></section><section id="compare" aria-label="Compare with another server" class="sp-panel cmp-box mt-8"><h2 class="sp-label">Compare with another server</h2><form class="mt-3 flex max-w-[620px] flex-wrap gap-2.5" action="/mcp/compare" method="get"><input type="hidden" name="a" value="dev.modelmarket/mcp-security"/><label for="cmp-with" class="sr-only">Registry name of the other server</label><input id="cmp-with" type="text" required="" minLength="2" maxLength="203" autoComplete="off" spellCheck="false" placeholder="Other server, e.g. io.github.owner/name" class="min-w-0 flex-1 rounded-md border border-rule bg-panel px-3 py-[11px] text-[15px] text-ink placeholder:text-ink-3" name="b"/><button type="submit" class="btn">Compare</button></form><p class="sp-note">Side by side: registry entry, our read-only session, the tools and the 18 classification fields. Same values as each page; no score.</p></section><p class="sp-part">Security testing</p><section id="tests" class="sp-sec" aria-labelledby="tests-h"><details class="sp-fold"><summary class="sp-head" id="tests-h"><h2 class="sp-q">What did we test, and what did we leave out?</h2><span class="sp-label">18 checks · features #1, #2</span></summary><p><span class="sp-verdict">Not probed (we call no server&#x27;s tools)</span></p><p class="sp-note">We connected and read what the server declares, but did not call its tools: ProtocolProbe calls no server&#x27;s tools for anything it publishes. This is our choice, not a block by the server.<!-- --> No security score is given; a check we did not run is never counted as passed.</p><div class="sp-panel sp-matrix-wrap"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2"><b class="text-sm">The 18 checks at a glance</b><span class="src">our test · <!-- -->2026-10-23</span></div><ol class="sp-matrix" aria-label="State of each of the 18 checks"><li class="sp-cell g-exercised" title="1 Inventory: exercised"><span aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="sr-only">Inventory<!-- -->: <!-- -->exercised</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-exercised" title="2 Hidden instructions: exercised"><span aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="sr-only">Hidden instructions<!-- -->: <!-- -->exercised</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-run" title="3 Real execution: not run · our policy"><span aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="sr-only">Real execution<!-- -->: <!-- -->not run · our policy</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-run" title="4 Secret leak: not run · nothing to check it against"><span aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="sr-only">Secret leak<!-- -->: <!-- -->not run · nothing to check it against</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-run" title="5 Internal addresses: not run · our policy"><span aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="sr-only">Internal addresses<!-- -->: <!-- -->not run · our policy</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-run" title="6 Unconfirmed changes: not run · our policy"><span aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="sr-only">Unconfirmed changes<!-- -->: <!-- -->not run · our policy</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-run" title="7 Bad input: not run · our policy"><span aria-hidden="true">7</span><span class="sr-only">Bad input<!-- -->: <!-- -->not run · our policy</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-run" title="8 Model requests: not run · nothing to check it against"><span aria-hidden="true">8</span><span class="sr-only">Model requests<!-- -->: <!-- -->not run · nothing to check it against</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-run" title="9 Sensitive questions: not run · nothing to check it against"><span aria-hidden="true">9</span><span class="sr-only">Sensitive questions<!-- -->: <!-- -->not run · nothing to check it against</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-run" title="10 Folder boundary: not run · our policy"><span aria-hidden="true">10</span><span class="sr-only">Folder boundary<!-- -->: <!-- -->not run · our policy</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-run" title="11 Log leaks: not run · nothing to check it against"><span aria-hidden="true">11</span><span class="sr-only">Log leaks<!-- -->: <!-- -->not run · nothing to check it against</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-run" title="12 Hidden content: not run · nothing to check it against"><span aria-hidden="true">12</span><span class="sr-only">Hidden content<!-- -->: <!-- -->not run · nothing to check it against</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-applicable" title="13 Fake assistant turns: not applicable"><span aria-hidden="true">13</span><span class="sr-only">Fake assistant turns<!-- -->: <!-- -->not applicable</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-applicable" title="14 Token passthrough: not applicable"><span aria-hidden="true">14</span><span class="sr-only">Token passthrough<!-- -->: <!-- -->not applicable</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-applicable" title="15 Token audience: not applicable"><span aria-hidden="true">15</span><span class="sr-only">Token audience<!-- -->: <!-- -->not applicable</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-run" title="16 Sign-in redirect: not run · our policy"><span aria-hidden="true">16</span><span class="sr-only">Sign-in redirect<!-- -->: <!-- -->not run · our policy</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-run" title="17 Consent handling: not testable from outside"><span aria-hidden="true">17</span><span class="sr-only">Consent handling<!-- -->: <!-- -->not testable from outside</span></li><li class="sp-cell g-not-applicable" title="18 Sign-in metadata: not applicable"><span aria-hidden="true">18</span><span class="sr-only">Sign-in metadata<!-- -->: <!-- -->not applicable</span></li></ol><p class="sp-legend"><span class="g-exercised"><i></i>2<!-- --> exercised</span><span class="g-not-run"><i></i>12<!-- --> not run (reason given)</span><span class="g-not-applicable"><i></i>4<!-- --> not applicable</span></p></div><p class="sp-intro">Each check ends in exactly one state: exercised, not run (with the reason), or not applicable (with the reason).<!-- --> <!-- -->2 of the 14 checks that apply to it were exercised.<!-- --> We do not publish security-check outcomes for named servers.</p><div class="sp-panel"><div><div class="sp-group">Exercised<!-- --> · <!-- -->2</div><ul class="sp-rows"><li><span class="n">1</span><span class="name">Inventory<br/><span class="src">tool-list</span></span><span class="why">Reads the declared tools, resources and prompts.</span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-exercised">exercised</span></span></li><li><span class="n">2</span><span class="name">Hidden instructions<br/><span class="src">description-poisoning</span></span><span class="why">Looks for hidden instructions in tool descriptions.</span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-exercised">exercised</span></span></li></ul></div><div><div class="sp-group">Not run, with the reason<!-- --> · <!-- -->12</div><ul class="sp-rows"><li><span class="n">3</span><span class="name">Real execution<br/><span class="src">real-execution</span></span><span class="why">Calls a tool and checks what really happens.<small>This check calls the server&#x27;s tools. ProtocolProbe calls no server&#x27;s tools for anything it publishes; an operator can run this check on their own server with our self-test command.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-run">not run · our policy</span></span></li><li><span class="n">4</span><span class="name">Secret leak<br/><span class="src">canary-leak</span></span><span class="why">Plants a fake secret and checks whether it leaks.<small>This check needs at least one successful tool call to have something to check, and no tool was called.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-run">not run · nothing to check it against</span></span></li><li><span class="n">5</span><span class="name">Internal addresses<br/><span class="src">ssrf</span></span><span class="why">Checks whether a tool can be steered to internal addresses.<small>This check calls the server&#x27;s tools. ProtocolProbe calls no server&#x27;s tools for anything it publishes; an operator can run this check on their own server with our self-test command.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-run">not run · our policy</span></span></li><li><span class="n">6</span><span class="name">Unconfirmed changes<br/><span class="src">write-without-confirmation</span></span><span class="why">Checks whether tools that change data act without asking.<small>This check calls the server&#x27;s tools. ProtocolProbe calls no server&#x27;s tools for anything it publishes; an operator can run this check on their own server with our self-test command.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-run">not run · our policy</span></span></li><li><span class="n">7</span><span class="name">Bad input<br/><span class="src">error-handling</span></span><span class="why">Sends bad input and watches how the server answers.<small>This check calls the server&#x27;s tools. ProtocolProbe calls no server&#x27;s tools for anything it publishes; an operator can run this check on their own server with our self-test command.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-run">not run · our policy</span></span></li><li><span class="n">8</span><span class="name">Model requests<br/><span class="src">sampling</span></span><span class="why">Checks whether the server asks the client&#x27;s model to act for it.<small>This check needs at least one successful tool call to have something to check, and no tool was called.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-run">not run · nothing to check it against</span></span></li><li><span class="n">9</span><span class="name">Sensitive questions<br/><span class="src">elicitation-sensitive-data</span></span><span class="why">Checks whether the server asks users for sensitive data.<small>This check needs at least one successful tool call to have something to check, and no tool was called.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-run">not run · nothing to check it against</span></span></li><li><span class="n">10</span><span class="name">Folder boundary<br/><span class="src">root-boundary</span></span><span class="why">Checks whether the server reaches outside the folders it was given.<small>This check calls the server&#x27;s tools. ProtocolProbe calls no server&#x27;s tools for anything it publishes; an operator can run this check on their own server with our self-test command.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-run">not run · our policy</span></span></li><li><span class="n">11</span><span class="name">Log leaks<br/><span class="src">logging-side-channel</span></span><span class="why">Checks whether log messages carry data they should not.<small>This check needs at least one successful tool call to have something to check, and no tool was called.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-run">not run · nothing to check it against</span></span></li><li><span class="n">12</span><span class="name">Hidden content<br/><span class="src">audience-hiding</span></span><span class="why">Checks resources that hide content from the user.<small>This check needs content the server returns, and nothing was read or called.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-run">not run · nothing to check it against</span></span></li><li><span class="n">16</span><span class="name">Sign-in redirect<br/><span class="src">open-redirect</span></span><span class="why">Checks the sign-in redirect for abuse.<small>Testing the sign-in redirect means sending probes to the operator&#x27;s sign-in service, which we do not do.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-run">not run · our policy</span></span></li><li><span class="n">17</span><span class="name">Consent handling<br/><span class="src">confused-deputy</span></span><span class="why">Checks consent handling when one service acts for another.<small>Depends on the operator&#x27;s own consent screen, which differs per server and cannot be tested from outside.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-run">not testable from outside</span></span></li></ul></div><div><div class="sp-group">Does not apply to this server<!-- --> · <!-- -->4</div><ul class="sp-rows"><li><span class="n">13</span><span class="name">Fake assistant turns<br/><span class="src">fake-assistant-turn</span></span><span class="why">Checks prompts that pose as the assistant&#x27;s own words.<small>The server exposes no prompts.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-applicable">not applicable</span></span></li><li><span class="n">14</span><span class="name">Token passthrough<br/><span class="src">token-passthrough</span></span><span class="why">Checks whether the server forwards a user&#x27;s token to other services.<small>The server opened a session without sign-in, so there is no token flow to check.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-applicable">not applicable</span></span></li><li><span class="n">15</span><span class="name">Token audience<br/><span class="src">token-audience-validation</span></span><span class="why">Checks whether tokens meant for another service are accepted.<small>The server opened a session without sign-in, so there is no token flow to check.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-applicable">not applicable</span></span></li><li><span class="n">18</span><span class="name">Sign-in metadata<br/><span class="src">oauth-url-scheme</span></span><span class="why">Checks the published sign-in metadata for unsafe URLs.<small>No sign-in (OAuth) metadata is published, so there are no sign-in addresses to check.</small></span><span class="st"><span class="sp-status g-not-applicable">not applicable</span></span></li></ul></div></div><p class="sp-note">Source: our own test<!-- -->, <!-- -->2026-10-23<!-- -->, mcp-runtime-engine@0.1.0<!-- -->. Which checks count and why follows our published scoring model.</p></details></section><section id="timeline" class="sp-sec" aria-labelledby="timeline-h"><details class="sp-fold"><summary class="sp-head" id="timeline-h"><h2 class="sp-q">What happened during the test?</h2><span class="sp-label">Feature #8</span></summary><p class="sp-intro">The steps in order, as the test record holds them.</p><ol class="sp-panel sp-timeline"><li><span class="t">0 ms</span><span class="d">Started a read-only session with the server&#x27;s remote endpoint</span></li><li><span class="t">531 ms</span><span class="d">Connected after 0 redirects. No credential was sent or needed.</span></li><li><span class="t"></span><span class="d">Read the inventory: 4 tools, 0 resources, 0 prompts.</span></li><li class="end"><span class="t">3,730 ms</span><span class="d">Finished: 2 checks exercised.</span></li></ol></details></section><p class="sp-part">Reference</p><section id="classification" class="sp-sec" aria-labelledby="classification-h"><details class="sp-fold" open=""><summary class="sp-head" id="classification-h"><h2 class="sp-q">How is it classified?</h2><span class="sp-label">18 fields</span></summary><p class="sp-intro">One value per field, each with its source. Fields written by AI models are marked. A field with no value says why.</p><div class="sp-tax"><div><div class="k"><span>Topic</span><span class="text-signal">AI-classified</span></div><div class="v"><a class="link" href="/mcp/servers/browse?topic=security" title="All servers with this value">security</a></div><div class="s">AI-classified · 2026-10-23</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>Pricing model</span><span class="text-signal">AI-classified</span></div><div class="v">free</div><div class="s">read from modelmarket.dev/tools/ · 2026-10-23</div><p class="sp-quote" data-pub="">“<!-- -->Free tools for developers<!-- -->”</p></div><div><div class="k"><span>Programming language</span></div><div class="v"><a class="link" href="/mcp/servers/browse?lang=TypeScript" title="All servers with this value">TypeScript</a></div><div class="s">api.github.com · 2026-10-23</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>Hosting type</span></div><div class="v"><a class="link" href="/mcp/servers/browse?runs=remote" title="All servers with this value">remote (hosted by the publisher)</a></div><div class="s">registry · 2026-10-23</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>MCP capability</span></div><div class="v">tools</div><div class="s">our test · 2026-10-23</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>Transport</span></div><div class="v">streamable HTTP</div><div class="s">registry · 2026-10-23</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>Required credentials</span></div><div class="v">none declared</div><div class="s">registry · no declaration is not a guarantee</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>Package registry</span></div><div class="v none">does not apply</div><div class="s">remote-only server: no package is shipped, so there is no package registry</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>Freshness</span></div><div class="v">0–30 days</div><div class="s">registry updatedAt · 2026-10-23</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>Lifecycle status</span></div><div class="v"><a class="link" href="/mcp/servers/browse?status=active" title="All servers with this value">active</a></div><div class="s">registry · 2026-10-23</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>License class</span></div><div class="v none">does not apply</div><div class="s">remote-only server: ships no package, so there is nothing to look up in a package registry</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>Integrity hash</span></div><div class="v none">does not apply</div><div class="s">remote-only server: ships no package, so there is nothing to look up in a package registry</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>Signature / provenance</span></div><div class="v none">does not apply</div><div class="s">remote-only server: ships no package, so there is nothing to look up in a package registry</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>Dependency advisories</span></div><div class="v none">does not apply</div><div class="s">ships no package, so there are no dependencies to audit</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>Popularity</span></div><div class="v none">does not apply</div><div class="s">remote-only server: ships no package, so there is nothing to look up in a package registry</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>Publisher signals</span></div><div class="v">owner: a personal account · repository age: 31–90 days · stars: 0–9</div><div class="s">api.github.com · 2026-10-22</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>Maintenance</span></div><div class="v"><a class="link" href="/mcp/servers/browse?maint=active" title="All servers with this value">active</a></div><div class="s">api.github.com · 2026-10-22</div></div><div><div class="k"><span>Environment</span></div><div class="v">the publisher&#x27;s infrastructure</div><div class="s">where it runs, from the hosting type</div></div></div><p class="sp-note">“Not stated” means the source did not state it; “does not apply” means it does not apply to this kind of server; “our limit” means our own lookup failed.<!-- --> A linked value opens the directory filtered to the same value.</p></details></section><section id="cite" class="sp-sec" aria-labelledby="cite-h"><details class="sp-fold" open=""><summary class="sp-head" id="cite-h"><h2 class="sp-q">Cite or correct this page</h2><span class="sp-label">Sources and corrections</span></summary><div class="sp-grid"><div class="sp-panel"><h4>Suggested citation</h4><p class="sp-pre">ProtocolProbe. “<!-- -->dev.modelmarket/mcp-security<!-- -->: MCP server record.” Data checked <!-- -->2026-10-23<!-- -->. <!-- -->https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/servers/dev.modelmarket/mcp-security</p><p class="sp-note">Figures are valid for the date shown. Our facts on this page are <a class="link" href="/terms">CC BY 4.0</a>: reuse them with a link and the check date. Quoted text (the publisher’s descriptions, website quotes, tool names) is not ours to license.</p><p class="sp-note">As JSON: <a class="link" href="/api/v1/servers/dev.modelmarket/mcp-security">this record in the API</a> · <a class="link" href="/docs/api">API documentation</a>.</p></div><div class="sp-panel"><h4>Badge for your README</h4><p class="mt-2"><img src="/api/v1/badge/dev.modelmarket/mcp-security" alt="ProtocolProbe: 5 of 5 record checks met" height="20" loading="lazy"/></p><p class="sp-pre mt-3">[![ProtocolProbe](https://protocolprobe.com/api/v1/badge/dev.modelmarket/mcp-security)](https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/servers/dev.modelmarket/mcp-security)</p><p class="sp-note">It shows this server&#x27;s <a class="link" href="#record-checks">record-check count</a>: facts from public records, no tool called. It is not a security rating or a pass. It links here and updates after each data reload.</p></div><div class="sp-panel"><h4>Something wrong, or is this yours?</h4><p class="text-sm text-ink-2">If a fact here is wrong, tell us and we will re-check it. If you operate this server, you can run our checks on it yourself with the free <a class="link" href="/docs/selftest">self-test command</a>; we call no server’s tools ourselves for anything shown here.</p><p class="mt-3 text-sm">Write to <a class="link" href="mailto:hello@protocolprobe.com?subject=Server%20page%3A%20dev.modelmarket%2Fmcp-security">hello@protocolprobe.com</a> · <a class="link" href="/corrections">corrections log</a> · <a class="link" href="/methodology">methodology</a></p></div></div></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="wrap pb-16 pt-9 text-[13px] text-ink-3"><nav aria-label="Site" class="grid gap-x-6 gap-y-7 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5"><section aria-labelledby="footer-choose" class="min-w-0"><p id="footer-choose" class="eyebrow">Choose a server</p><ul class="mt-2 grid gap-1.5"><li><a href="/mcp/servers/search" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Search by name or description</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/tools" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Search MCP tools by name</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/page/1#filters" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Browse and filter every server</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/tested/1" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Servers we opened live (read-only)</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/top" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Rankings: downloads, stars, record checks</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/compared" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Most downloaded and starred, compared by topic</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/compare" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Compare two servers</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/same-tools" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Servers with the same tools</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/publishers" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Servers by publisher</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/tool-type/changes-data/1" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Servers whose tools change data</a></li></ul></section><section aria-labelledby="footer-yours" class="min-w-0"><p id="footer-yours" class="eyebrow">Test your own server</p><ul class="mt-2 grid gap-1.5"><li><a href="/docs/selftest" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Self-test command</a></li><li><a href="/docs/selftest#url" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Test your server at its URL</a></li><li><a href="/docs/selftest#credential" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">A server that needs a token</a></li><li><a href="/docs/selftest#ci" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Run it in CI (GitHub code scanning)</a></li><li><a href="/docs/record-checks" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">How record checks are counted</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/search" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Your server’s page and README badge</a></li><li><a href="/docs/discover" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Discover servers on your machine</a></li></ul></section><section aria-labelledby="footer-data" class="min-w-0"><p id="footer-data" class="eyebrow">Use the data</p><ul class="mt-2 grid gap-1.5"><li><a href="/docs/api" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">API (no key)</a></li><li><a href="/docs/cite" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Dataset and how to cite</a></li><li><a href="/feed.xml" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Feed: reports, updates, corrections</a></li><li><a href="/llms.txt" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">llms.txt for AI tools</a></li></ul></section><section aria-labelledby="footer-understand" class="min-w-0"><p id="footer-understand" class="eyebrow">Understand the registry</p><ul class="mt-2 grid gap-1.5"><li><a href="/mcp/numbers" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">MCP in numbers: every figure, with charts</a></li><li><a href="/updates/three-models" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Tool lists at three AI models</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/reports/registry-vs-reality" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Main report</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/reports/catalogue" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">What is in the registry</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/reports/not-tested" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Why some servers are not tested</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/changes" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Changes: registry and re-checked facts</a></li><li><a href="/mcp/servers/removed" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Servers removed from the registry</a></li><li><a href="/methodology" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Methodology</a></li><li><a href="/updates" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Updates</a></li><li><a href="/corrections" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Corrections log</a></li></ul></section><section aria-labelledby="footer-about" class="min-w-0"><p id="footer-about" class="eyebrow">About</p><ul class="mt-2 grid gap-1.5"><li><a href="/about" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">About</a></li><li><a href="/contact" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Contact</a></li><li><a href="/newsletter" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Newsletter</a></li><li><a href="/security" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Security &amp; disclosure</a></li><li><a href="/privacy" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Privacy</a></li><li><a href="/terms" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">Terms</a></li><li><a href="/.well-known/security.txt" class="text-ink-2 no-underline hover:text-ink">security.txt</a></li></ul></section></nav><p class="mt-8 font-mono">© <!-- -->ProtocolProbe<!-- --> · base snapshot <!-- -->2026-10-23<!-- --> · updated daily, <a href="/mcp/changes" class="text-ink-2 hover:text-ink">what changed</a></p></footer><script defer="" src="/f3921f489ceb0a40/script.js" data-sdkn="@vercel/analytics" data-view-endpoint="/f3921f489ceb0a40/view" data-event-endpoint="/f3921f489ceb0a40/event" data-session-endpoint="/f3921f489ceb0a40/session"></script></div></body></html>